y substance which is used to reduce or control weight.【45†metabolite】  Any intermediate or product resulting from metabolism.\nL67: The term 'metabolite' subsumes the classes commonly known as primary and secondary metabolites.【46†anti-HIV agent】  An antiviral agent that destroys or inhibits the replication of the human immunodeficiency virus.【47†mouse metabolite】  Any mammalian metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in a mouse (Mus musculus).【48†Escherichia coli metabolite】  Any bacterial metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in Escherichia coli.【49†EC 3.5.1.19 (nicotinamidase) inhibitor】  An EC 3.5.1.* (non-peptide linear amide C-N hydrolase) inhibitor that interferes with the action of nicotinamidase (EC 3.5.1.19).【50†plant metabolite】  Any eukaryotic metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in plants, the kingdom that include flowering plants, conifers and other gymnosperms.【51†antitubercular agent】  A substance that kills or slows the growth of Mycobacterium tuberculosis and is used in the treatment of tuberculosis.【52†human urinary metabolite】  Any metabolite (endogenous or exogenous) found in human urine samples.【53†analgesic】  An agent capable of relieving pain without the loss of consciousness or without producing anaesthesia.\nL68: In addition, analgesic is a role played by a compound which is exhibited by a capability to cause a reduction of pain symptoms.【54†water-soluble vitamin (role)】  Any vitamin that dissolves in water and readily absorbed into tissues for immediate use.\nL69: Unlike the fat-soluble vitamins, they are not stored in the body and need to be replenished regularly in the diet and will rarely accumulate to toxic levels since they are quickly excreted from the body via urine.【45†metabolite】  Any intermediate or product resulting from metabolism. The term 'metabolite' subsumes the classes commonly known as primary and secondary metabolites.\nL70: 【55†Application s:】  | 【56†antilipemic drug】  A substance used to treat hyperlipidemia (an excess of lipids in the blood).【57†antipsychotic agent】  Antipsychotic drugs are agents that control agitated psychotic behaviour, alleviate acute psychotic states, reduce psychotic symptoms, and exert a quieting effect.【58†hypoglycemic agent】  A drug which lowers the blood glucose level.【59†anticholesteremic drug】  A substance used to lower plasma cholesterol levels.【60†antineoplastic agent】  A substance that inhibits or prevents the proliferation of neoplasms.【61†antidote】  Any protective agent counteracting or neutralizing the action of poisons.【62†vasodilator agent】  A drug used to cause dilation of the blood vessels.【63†renoprotective agent】  Any compound that is able to prevent damage to the kidneys.【64†antidepressant】  Antidepressants are mood-stimulating drugs used primarily in the treatment of affective disorders and related conditions.【65†cardiovascular drug】  A drug that affects the rate or intensity of cardiac contraction, blood vessel diameter or blood volume.【66†antiatherosclerotic agent】  A cardiovascular drug that prevents atherosclerosis (a disease in which the inside of an artery narrows due to the build up of plaque).\nL71: Compare with 【67†antiatherogenic agent】.【68†anxiolytic drug】  Anxiolytic drugs are agents that alleviate anxiety, tension, and anxiety disorders, promote sedation, and have a calming effect without affecting clarity of consciousness or neurologic conditions.【51†antitubercular agent】  A substance that kills or slows the growth of Mycobacterium tuberculosis and is used in the treatment of tuberculosis.【69†anti-anaemic agent】  A compound which increases either the number of red cells or the amount of haemoglobin in the blood.【53†analgesic】  An agent capable of relieving pain without the loss of consciousness or without producing anaesthesia.\nL72: In addition, analgesic is a role played by a compound which is exhibited by a capability to cause a reduction of pain symptoms.【70†nutraceutical】  A product in capsule, tablet or liquid form that provide essential nutrients, such as a vitamin, an essential mineral, a protein, an herb, or similar nutritional substance.\nL73: ChEBI Ontology\nL74: ---\nL75: \nL76: Text\nL77: \nL78: Tree View\nL79: \nL80: Graph View\nL81: Outgoing Relation(s)\nL82: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role Escherichia coli metabolite (【48†CHEBI:76971】)\nL83: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role analgesic (【53†CHEBI:35480】)\nL84: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role anti-anaemic agent (【69†CHEBI:75835】)\nL85: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role anti-HIV agent (【46†CHEBI:64946】)\nL86: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role anti-obesity agent (【44†CHEBI:74518】)\nL87: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role antiatherosclerotic agent (【66†CHEBI:145947】)\nL88: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role anticholesteremic drug (【59†CHEBI:35821】)\nL89: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role antidepressant (【64†CHEBI:35469】)\nL90: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role antidote (【61†CHEBI:50247】)\nL91: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role antilipemic drug (【56†CHEBI:35679】)\nL92: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role antineoplastic agent (【60†CHEBI:35610】)\nL93: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role antipsychotic agent (【57†CHEBI:35476】)\nL94: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role antitubercular agent (【51†CHEBI:33231】)\nL95: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role anxiolytic drug (【68†CHEBI:35474】)\nL96: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role cardiovascular drug (【65†CHEBI:35554】)\nL97: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role EC 3.5.1.19 (nicotinamidase) inhibitor (【49†CHEBI:84264】)\nL98: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role human urinary metabolite (【52†CHEBI:84087】)\nL99: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role hypoglycemic agent (【58†CHEBI:35526】)\nL100: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role metabolite (【45†CHEBI:25212】)\nL101: nicotinic acid (【71†CHEBI:15940】) has role mou