e, lycine and oxyneurine.\nL209: \nL210: ### Application\nL211: \nL212: Betaine has been used to study the effects of antioxidants on regrowth from cryopreservation.\nL213: ### Biochem/physiol Actions\nL214: \nL215: End-product of oxidative metabolism of choline, betaine is a general methyl donor, in particular in a minor pathway of methionine biosynthesis. It is used to treat homocystinuria, which is a defect in the major pathway of methionine biosynthesis.\nL216: Apart from betaine taking part in transmethylation, it acts as an organic osmolyte in protecting cells under stress. This is being significantly observed in plants and microorganisms. Betaine is also known to increase the levels of S-adenosylmethionine and thus this might reduce the effects of hepatic steatosis.\nL217: \nL218: * * *\nL219: ## Compare Similar Items\nL220: \nL221: 【18†View Full Comparison】\nL222: \nL223: * * *\nL224: \nL225: Show Differences\nL226: \nL227: [Input]\nL228: \nL229: 1 of 1\nL230: ###### This Item\nL231:  | 61962  | 1065695  | B0300\nL232: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL233: 【19†Sigma-Aldrich B2629 Betaine】[Button: Quick View]  | 【20†Sigma-Aldrich 61962 Betaine】[Button: Quick View]  | 【21†USP 1065695 Betaine】[Button: Quick View]  | 【22†Sigma-Aldrich B0300 Betaine solution】[Button: Quick View]\nL234: description≥98% (perchloric acid titration)  | description BioUltra, ≥99.0% (NT)  | description United States Pharmacopeia (USP) Reference Standard  | description 5 M, PCR Reagent\nL235: assay≥98% (perchloric acid titration)  | assay≥99.0% (NT)  | assay-  | assay-\nL236: biological source sugar beets  | biological source-  | biological source-  | biological source-\nL237: Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 200  | Quality Level-  | Quality Level 300\nL238: form powder or crystals  | form-  | form-  | form liquid\nL239: storage temp.2-8°C  | storage temp.-  | storage temp.-  | storage temp.2-8°C\nL240: solubility water: 50 mg/mL, clear, colorless to faintly yellow  | solubility methanol: 1 M 